<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis II of Italy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 825–875</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Louis II, Holy Roman Emperor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair I</a>, king of Italy from 844 and Carolingian emperor from 855. When his father's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Francia</a> was divided he received Italy, and he shared Provence with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-ii">Lothair II</a>. He spent much of his reign fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> in southern Italy and captured their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> in 871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-ii-of-italy.jpg" alt="Louis II of Italy" width="237" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Berardi (chronicon casauriense) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_II_of_Italy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
